functions.doc:
One run's wall, read one row at a time.

The mesh changes with the run -- every capsule has its own node coordinates -- so the file is read row by row;
``get_field`` across several rows is refused by the format for exactly that reason.

Train on the older part of the record, evaluate and optimize on the newest part. The L2 regularisation
of the KPI model is chosen by forward-chaining cross-validation inside the training part (``cv_folds``;
0 keeps the default) and the fold errors go in the report under ``model.cv``.

classes.doc:
Several bundles as an iterable of dictionaries -- the shape a PhysicsNeMo loop iterates.

``tensors=True`` converts to ``torch`` tensors when torch is installed, which is what a training loop wants;
without it the dictionaries carry numpy arrays, which is still a legal map-style dataset.
